The satellite-only gravity field model GOCO2025s
================================================
These data are freely available under the Creative Commons Attribution
4.0 International Licence (CC BY 4.0)
When using the data please cite:

Oehlinger, Felix; Mayer-Guerr, Torsten; Krauss, Sandro;
Dumitraschkewitz, Patrick; Suesser-Rechberger, Barbara; Strasser, Andreas;
Tieber-Hubmann, Cornelia; Brockmann, Jan Martin (2025):
The satellite-only gravity field model GOCO2025s.
Data set. Graz University of Technology. https://doi.org/10.3217/f48p8-8h651

A gravity field functional at time t can be computed with

 V(t) = gfct
      + trnd    * (t-t0)/T
      + acos1.0 * cos(2pi*(t-t0)/T) + asin1.0 * sin(2pi*(t-t0)/T)
      + acos0.5 * cos(4pi*(t-t0)/T) + asin0.5 * sin(4pi*(t-t0)/T)

with the reference epoch t0 = 57023 MJD (2015-01-01) and
the annual period T = 365.25 d.

The model contains the gravitational potential of the complete Earth,
including non-tidal atmospheric and ocean masses.
It can be used as a stand-alone model. To be used together with
the 3-hourly Ocean and Dealiasing Model AOD1B, the long time components
present in both AOD1B and GOCO2025s must be reduced beforehand:

 V_full(t) = GOCO2025s(t)
           + AOD1B_RL06(t) - AOD1B_RL06_included_in_GOCO2025s(t),
or

 V_full(t) = GOCO2025s(t)
           + AOD1B_RL07(t) - AOD1B_RL07_included_in_GOCO2025s(t).

AOD1B_RL0X_included_in_GOCO2025s.gfc can be downloaded
at the TU Graz repository: https://doi.org/10.3217/f48p8-8h651

GOCO2025s is a satellite-only, global gravity field model
up to degree and order 300, with constrained secular, annual, and semi-annual
variations up to degree and order 200. This solution is estimated from data
covering the period from 2002 to 2024 (inclusive):
 - GOCE: TIM6 Gradiometer observations
 - GRACE
 - GRACE-FO: including KBR and LRI observations
 - Kinematic orbits:
     CHAMP, GOCE, Swarm A+B+C, Sentinel-1A/1B/2A/2B/3A/3B/6A,
     TerraSAR-X, TanDEM-X,
 - SLR (ITRF2020 reference frame):
     AJISAI, BLITS, LAGEOS1, LAGEOS2, LARES, LARES2, LARETS, Starlette, Stella
 - Regularization: Kaula degree >150.
The temporal variations include observations up to degree and order 150
and are regularized using isotropic noise, separated by land/ocean masks,
up to degree and order 200.

GOCO (Gravity Observation Combination) is an initiative with the objective
of computing high-accuracy and high-resolution static global gravity field
models (www.goco.eu).

